    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n11898" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cunctābundus</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cont-</span></b> ), a, um,
			adj.
		cunctor, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>lingering, loitering, delaying</i> (very rare): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">(milites) cunctabundosque et resistentes
					egressos castris esse,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv.
					6, 7, 2</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">nusquam cunctabundus nisi cum in senatu
					loqueretur,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tac. A.
					1, 7</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">verba,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Mamert. in Jul. 18, 6</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">amnis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Eum. Pan. Const. 18, 3</span></i>
			.</div>
